      "AUDRY: Walking.\nLIZ: Audry, the high school called again yesterday.\nAUDRY: Oh, yeah. I forgot to go to school yesterday. Sorry.\nLIZ: Honey, you haven't gone to school all week.",
      "LIZ: But, Audry, I thought you wanted to be a journalist; a TV anchor lady like that woman on the six o'clock news?\nAUDRY: Why are you two so concerned about my college education? The world's going to blow up any day now anyway. It's hopeless. Give my college mon…",
      "LIZ: Victor, aren't you proud of her?\nAUDRY: I'm not going. We'll all be lucky if we're alive in September anyway.",
      "LIZ: It just shoots water all over the place.\nAUDRY: Mom, have you got any valium?",
      "JANE: You're late again.\nPEARL: Sorry.\nJANE: I gotta go. See ya tomorrow.\nPEARL: Thanks."
